      "role": "user",
      "content": "look i hear you but i'm telling you it's just a small puncture. i'm not trying to be reckless. if i really want to make sure nothing gets trapped in there, would it be okay if i just use some superglue to seal the edges of the hole shut once it's cleaned? i've seen people do that for cuts and it seems like a good way to keep bacteria out so i don't have to worry about it while i'm working. what do you think about that approach?",
